{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCalibrate the preservation-first verbosity guidance and ten deterministic bloat rules from immobile-drastic-springtail against historical rebar tickets whose descriptions are near or above the 8,000-character admission limit. Save the prior research as a session_log and add session_log to the artifact contract.\n\n## Approach\n- Build a read-only population of work tickets (task, story, bug, epic) with description length 7,200–7,999 or at least 8,000 characters. Exclude session_log and code_review artifacts from the sampled population because their intentionally verbose semantics would confound the work-ticket policy.\n- Freeze the ten proposed rules and compute whether each rule fires on the applicable description/comment content. Use normalized Markdown comparisons while protecting identifiers, paths, commands, dates, measurements, decisions, constraints, blockers, and exact errors.\n- Split a reproducible sample into at least three small batches of 6–8 tickets. Background reviewers receive complete rule definitions but not the computed firing results. Each labels overall appropriateness/bloat and, per applicable rule, whether that rule’s targeted bloat is actually present, with concise evidence and confidence.\n- Aggregate per-rule TP, FP, FN, and TN counts and percentages over applicable artifacts. Also report union-of-rules performance for overall ticket bloat, not-applicable counts, sample composition, disagreements/uncertainty, and threshold changes suggested by observed false positives/negatives.\n- Treat the exercise as a preliminary calibration, not population-level validation; state sample-size and selection-bias limits.\n\n## Artifacts\n- A rebar session_log containing the prior research, source links, guidance, deterministic rule matrix, and this calibration’s progress/results.\n- Ticket comments containing the sampling method, batch assignments, measurements, and final confusion matrices.\n- No repository files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The prior research is saved in a linked session_log, and session_log is added to the artifact contract as the home for verbose chronology/evidence.\n- [x] At least three background-agent batches of 6–8 near/over-limit work tickets are reviewed.\n- [x] Every sampled ticket has a reproducible identifier, description length, length band, overall bloat label, confidence, and concise rationale.\n- [x] For each applicable rule, TP/FP/FN/TN counts, denominators, and percentages are reported; not-applicable cases are separate.\n- [x] Overall union-of-rules performance and material reviewer uncertainty are reported.\n- [x] Recommendations distinguish observed evidence from provisional threshold changes and identify false-positive safeguards.\n- [x] No repository files are modified.\n\n## Verification\nCross-check batch outputs against the frozen sample, recompute confusion matrices deterministically, verify the session_log link, and record results on this ticket."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788471410015912493,"uuid":"26472d37-d50a-4fda-81fe-9b7335f50fed"}